            <description><![CDATA[<h2>ChainLink 0.3.668</h2>
<p class="sub">A small follow-up to 0.3.665.</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Fixed duplicate events.</strong> An event could appear twice in Upcoming
  Events after a sync — the duplicate now removes itself on launch, and it can't
  happen again.</li>
  <li>The training plan's "longest ride" stat now says what it is — your longest
  <em>recent</em> ride — and shows the date it happened.</li>
  <li>Career Bests load instantly after the first visit instead of re-reading your
  whole history every time.</li>
  <li>Includes everything from 0.3.665 — the fitness signature that follows your
  training, breakthrough badges, career bests, and zoom-scoped graph averages.</li>
</ul>

<h3>A note about Strava</h3>
<p>As of 30 June 2026, Strava requires an <strong>active Strava subscription</strong>
for the API access ChainLink's Strava connection uses. If your subscription has
lapsed, the connection will stop working — that's Strava's change, not a ChainLink
bug, and the app now says so plainly instead of showing "Connected" next to an
error. If you sync through <strong>Garmin Connect</strong> you're unaffected, and
it remains the recommended way to get rides in.</p>
]]></description>
